{"title":"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(AI_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (AI solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution(In_Chinese)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution(In Chinese)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_with_discussion_of_a_generalized_case\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution with discussion of a generalized case</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_simple\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution simple</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Analytic_geometry_solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Analytic geometry solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/5/a252cc19c08fe62efc73a6ae674fc651405ca92f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB &lt; AC &lt; BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"15\" />. Let the incentre and incircle of triangle\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the point on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> different from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that the line\nthrough <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. Similarly, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the point on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> different from\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> such that the line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d7d48553f4d9e7ab418118607ea324cbfddfda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\omega$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> intersect the circumcircle of\ntriangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/2/c725c31d3b02df772959c7a80491d1ae896abf1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P  \\neq A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be the midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, respectively.\nProve that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/99933d2db31099325249e16a5ac241543ae2130b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle KIL + \\angle YPX = 180^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"193\" height=\"16\" />\n.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/oAB56KgGrXQ\">https://youtu.be/oAB56KgGrXQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/WnZv3fdpFXo\">https://youtu.be/WnZv3fdpFXo</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28AI_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(AI_solution)\">Video Solution (AI solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (AI solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/cjnJ6EXKWW4\">https://youtu.be/cjnJ6EXKWW4</a>\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution.28In_Chinese.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution(In_Chinese)\">Video Solution(In Chinese)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution(In Chinese)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/QphkkutmY5M\">https://youtu.be/QphkkutmY5M</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_3\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Part 1: Derive tangent values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/943ee9dfab75e22a8e9404d8eebd4eb7021ff4be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AIL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbe83c38eee321fb533e8cd55401f38b8e823d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AIK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" /> with trig values of angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/1/0a1352d1b32ec30e62432ad8c7ac1a47d1d6ef44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{A}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"16\" height=\"38\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/416d7a2fd742e12560d3d780b1cb600cc67452dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{B}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"17\" height=\"37\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/9/fd906fcca291c70fcc02d3cca89d7070878faf66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{C}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/p_AmooMMln4\">https://youtu.be/p_AmooMMln4</a>\n</p><p>Part 2: Derive tangent values <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/d/46de40470b4d613e22dc0604558055d1761a99a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XPM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5203f14e8f9412a0425c7ec4980b20cd220e05.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle YPM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"63\" height=\"14\" /> with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/MgrghZ2ESAg\">https://youtu.be/MgrghZ2ESAg</a>\n</p><p>Part 3: Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/a/48a1d3beef4a677fe7d440f698cacb949ceb042d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AIL + \\angle XPM = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"186\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/d/5ad2e6950d0009701c98a77656e3b6d6f085cc4f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AIK + \\angle YPM = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"188\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/iOp9mnmZyzU\">https://youtu.be/iOp9mnmZyzU</a>\n</p><p>Comments: Although this is an IMO problem, the skills needed to solve this problem have all previously tested in AMC and its system math contests, such as HMMT.~ also proved by Kislay Kai\n</p><p>Evidence 1: 2020 Spring HMMT Geometry Round Problem 8\n</p><p>I used the property that because point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on the angle bisector <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac056ce386c7154c5ed723c55b2808cc0357fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BPC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is isosceles. This is a crucial step to analyze <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/9/ff98dd5ffb7fb0cf738189f94fc594507086b01b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle XPY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" />. This technique was previously tested in this HMMT problem.\n</p><p>Evidence 2: 2022 AMC 12A Problem 25\n</p><p>The technique in this AMC problem can be easily and directly applied to this IMO problem to quickly determine the locations of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. If you read my solutions to both this AMC problem and this IMO problem, you will find that I simply took exactly the same approach to solve both.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_with_discussion_of_a_generalized_case\">Video Solution with discussion of a generalized case</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution with discussion of a generalized case\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/NJc79Ccg82E?si=J0YdHAz-46miJIO2\">https://youtu.be/NJc79Ccg82E?si=J0YdHAz-46miJIO2</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_simple\">Solution simple</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution simple\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2024_AIME_II_12_d.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e3/2024_AIME_II_12_d.png/330px-2024_AIME_II_12_d.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"330\" height=\"339\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e3/2024_AIME_II_12_d.png/495px-2024_AIME_II_12_d.png 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/e/e3/2024_AIME_II_12_d.png/660px-2024_AIME_II_12_d.png 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>Let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/6/8d65ee4be3c5a147392f610a76da254b42a87842.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$YZ||AB, XZ||AC, G \\in AC, IG||BC, G&#39; \\in AB, IG&#39; || BC.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"442\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2fe0d23da6c142211eb392657e6ba3f31e1410d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F= AC \\cap YZ, F&#39; = AB \\cap XZ.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"250\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4ac3790d0ab3f2940b31d4ec392aba5f83cbc537.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFZF&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> is the parallelogram with equal heights, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/c/4ac3790d0ab3f2940b31d4ec392aba5f83cbc537.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AFZF&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> is rhomb <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/4/ef48ac956824fcaea163a530a717e6df694aa006.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"41\" height=\"9\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/2/3e2e84321ad6dcae9e46fda9c558c4b615ef84f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle CAZ = \\angle AZY = \\angle BCP, AI = IZ.\\]\" width=\"292\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/9/969b3727f4a47afd2fd4f89e9030549cd33477b1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AL = LC, AI = IZ \\implies IL || ZC \\implies \\angle LIG = \\angle BCZ.\\]\" width=\"444\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/213b05ed731167d4fb388a800c05ecfd8e97bcb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AZY = \\angle BCP = \\angle YCP \\implies$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"261\" height=\"14\" /> points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/3/9a376ac12a4463d818411b5d014e111beade2ce4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C,P, Y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"60\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> are concyclic.\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/8/448e41c127087ef6fb748dbacc93d743b02e3dba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ZPY = \\angle LIG.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"135\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/1/eb1e410f4c87a001de6eb640aefe2e6536fc1a31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ZPX = \\angle KIG&#39;. \\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"160\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_4\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6J7KH778ptg\">https://youtu.be/6J7KH778ptg</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Analytic_geometry_solution\">Analytic geometry solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Analytic geometry solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use the following coordinate parametrization:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/f/faf921d810d2a98ad26626b01d82823ef325aa03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A=(0,1),\\qquad B=(-b,0),\\qquad C=(c,0),\\]\" width=\"334\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>where\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/5/d855c92a677fea016225637a4068da78d33a3279.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[b=\\frac12\\left(t^{-1}-t\\right),\\qquad c=\\frac12\\left(s^{-1}-s\\right).\\]\" width=\"289\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The incenter is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/6/7e68c2e2f7243105bc1566cdd3615a2f6b4d0e24.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[I=(i,j)=\\left(\\frac{t-s}{2},\\frac{1-st}{2}\\right).\\]\" width=\"227\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Hence the reflection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/8/4782e7c0ec2e25bdeb1c2f36f5ee7aa2da562d41.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[A&#39;=2I-A=(t-s,-st).\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, we also have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/0966e2e18f2a1e1fae375c3ff5e3ea52f8bb6334.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[K=\\left(\\frac c2,\\frac12\\right).\\]\" width=\"107\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> has slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/c/90c2296890442b778e4cb8e57768606522e5d539.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"28\" height=\"20\" />, the line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/6/2165d6dd8966ab2d738ad7dfd6c6333ec7f78300.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y+st=b^{-1}\\bigl(x-(t-s)\\bigr).\\]\" width=\"200\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Intersecting this line with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/8/2c8192806d71e21b6aadbc62745047157374c83b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[Y=(bst+t-s,0).\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> has equation\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/e/bbec227929d043b8e416229755c0734af70b0190.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2+y^2+(b-c)x+(bc-1)y-bc=0.\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Parametrize the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> by\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/2/962afe2b25d5a6727d1e0c657fde397f84f92b7e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x,y)=\\left(\\frac{\\lambda(t-s)}2,\\,1-\\frac{\\lambda(1+st)}2\\right).\\]\" width=\"281\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Substitution into the circle equation reduces to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/9/e095eb79bc1835593e75eb94ee4f8096e079497d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{(1+s^2)(1+t^2)}4\\,\\lambda \\left(\\lambda-\\frac{1+st}{2st}\\right)=0.\\]\" width=\"285\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>The two roots are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/8/ab8ccbedc8ad9dd3e5fb8e654b94ee38f70f19e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lambda=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, corresponding to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/8/fc88b1a90510cfeb0a45a085e586f718fbf419d4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lambda=\\frac{1+st}{2st}.\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Thus the second intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> with the circumcircle is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/58245ade522c9c82a9fa4469af062ce6c8cd671e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[P=\\left(\\frac{(t-s)(1+st)}{4st}, -\\frac{(1-st)^2}{4st}\\right).\\]\" width=\"281\" height=\"43\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/4/e24f8a5f5bc137222c62f4960ac79c6fbecf41a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y_y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"54\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c506fd26d6c8655abce6487670d1f5190a92257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P_x=(c-b)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"116\" height=\"20\" />, we obtain\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/d/53d3ea21ae95d17c10c52fad9b1fbe1518b9dbba.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[k_{PY} =\\frac{-\\dfrac{(1-st)^2}{4st}} {\\dfrac{c-b}{2}-(bst+t-s)} =\\frac{(1-st)^2} {2s^2t(1-t^2)+(t-s)(3st-1)}.\\]\" width=\"486\" height=\"81\" />\n</p><p>Next we compute the angle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Applying the tangent subtraction formula to the directions of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64f70416d14a373677c13bb4a45d204e5229a1ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IA$\" width=\"23\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/6/f8631a9a7518bf0907936d1e96defe9cf7c19cef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IK$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, with the clockwise orientation used in the figure, gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/2/d7203a14b509fbcd77060923a8acb6a9f55284e7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan\\angle AIK =-\\frac{\\dfrac{1-j}{i}+\\dfrac{2j-1}{2i-c}} {1-\\dfrac{(1-j)(2j-1)}{i(2i-c)}} =-\\frac{i+(j-1)c} {2(i^2+j^2)-ci-3j+1}.\\]\" width=\"505\" height=\"86\" />\n</p><p>We now put both expressions into a common algebraic form. Define\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/328e36c8d756ecdcbf131302cb9881b675a856b0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f_1=(1-st)^2,\\]\" width=\"112\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/f/6cf73793401f42767cf53d581bf085640ceb8cf7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g_1=2s^2t(1-t^2)+(t-s)(3st-1).\\]\" width=\"278\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>A direct factorization gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db4d395f5b4d9965288fc00097e922e92e663c7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g_1=(1-st)(2st^2+s-t).\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Also define\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/0/1803708a1294d19dc1c9af4b550910b8a9d51373.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f_2=(1+st)(s^{-1}-s)-2(t-s) =(1-st)(s+s^{-1}),\\]\" width=\"414\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/6/1b61b1e0786c308be9c4dce9ab8108c832e0ff96.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g_2 =2\\bigl(s^2t^2+s^2+t^2+1-4st\\bigr) -6(1-st)-(t-s)(s^{-1}-s)+4.\\]\" width=\"519\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Substituting\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/6/b46928e80905f418b8fe82a6911b0a5aa0032c88.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[i=\\frac{t-s}{2},\\qquad j=\\frac{1-st}{2},\\qquad c=\\frac{s^{-1}-s}{2}\\]\" width=\"328\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>into the preceding angle formula gives\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/8/748a2a80870748c4dadb7e2be0d513e3af695065.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan\\angle AIK=\\frac{f_2}{g_2}.\\]\" width=\"130\" height=\"41\" />\n</p><p>It remains to identify <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/0/a6053907b455e0ef20a366e07f007ac4fc0eb002.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />. Let\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/9/43928d8c3b09387747d22e9a173cf40de6067009.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\widetilde g_2(t) =(s+s^{-1})(2st^2+s-t).\\]\" width=\"241\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>For fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/8/d98b95a0c2dde2e2e613e82c9c37734e78737c22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g_2(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/0/590cb65e1523e371f74c79871367cedc25606910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\widetilde g_2(t)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"20\" /> are quadratic polynomials in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />. They agree at two points:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/f/70f70b88e9391c782560e5a3215508b980957263.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g_2(0)=s^2+1=\\widetilde g_2(0),\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>and\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/f/5bfd362d35fc7f77f9f5aef21c8cda17f2280b4c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g_2(s^{-1}) =(s+s^{-1})^2 =\\widetilde g_2(s^{-1}).\\]\" width=\"244\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Moreover, they have the same leading coefficient, since\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d05636d78ba17aeefd3d242ac540e4727cd810b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac12\\frac{\\partial^2g_2}{\\partial t^2} =2(s^2+1) =\\frac12\\frac{\\partial^2\\widetilde g_2}{\\partial t^2}.\\]\" width=\"223\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, by interpolation for quadratic polynomials,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a153bd7024e279546ad9aff98c6cc86ef6a737f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[g_2=\\widetilde g_2 =(s+s^{-1})(2st^2+s-t).\\]\" width=\"260\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Consequently,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/1/2717aaa0901750cd5fae39908a66fbea9369042d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{f_1}{g_1} =\\frac{1-st}{2st^2+s-t} =\\frac{(1-st)(s+s^{-1})} {(s+s^{-1})(2st^2+s-t)} =\\frac{f_2}{g_2}.\\]\" width=\"390\" height=\"44\" />\n</p><p>Hence\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/1/ee1bfa103dc34a0faf27de6c3e240e3304006501.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tan\\angle AIK=k_{PY}.\\]\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Both angles are taken in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/1/58120b09b09030f8626fa6fe4ccdccdd3c11654d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0,\\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"18\" />, so the inclination of the ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/0/a0080013cb20903a6f4e80fa9450edd707894926.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PY$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> to the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/b/e2bbe83c38eee321fb533e8cd55401f38b8e823d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AIK$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"54\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Repeating the same calculation after interchanging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />—equivalently, reflecting the coordinate picture in the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-axis and interchanging <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce58e4af225c93d08606c26554caaa5ae32edeba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />—shows that the inclination of the ray <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05fc2c59d25e97ec515446444b44cbe415d3f383.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX$\" width=\"29\" height=\"12\" /> to the positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />-axis is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/7/6b7a8c38859fdb5449c3fcbb0c271f5acd16f47e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\pi-\\angle AIL.\\]\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Therefore\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc833b22043107e52dd6082f843f31183b8ade.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle YPX =\\pi-\\angle AIL-\\angle AIK =\\pi-\\angle KIL.\\]\" width=\"351\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>Thus\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/8/da8830b9d58d084fe40a5f9f82d94d0c8227ffd6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\angle KIL+\\angle YPX=180^\\circ}.\\]\" width=\"205\" height=\"26\" />\n</p><p><b>by IntuiMath</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO\" title=\"2024 IMO\">2024 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2024_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2024 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018030146\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.060 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.088 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 700/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 23252/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.173      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.173      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:28213:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018030146 and revision id 291155. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}